```

This class provides a proof-of-concept for Pex's handling of `[PexAssumeUnderTest]`. The `[PexObserve.ValueForViewingAttribute]` is used to observe the state of the `arrLsit`, `Old_x`, `Old_index`, `Old_arrListIndexOfX`, `New_arrListIndexOfX`, `Old_arrListLastIndexOfX`, `New_arrListLastIndexOfX`, `Old_arrListContainsX`, and `New_arrListContainsX`.

The test method asserts that `New_arrListIndexOfX <= Old_index`. There is also a call to `arrList.Remove()` to make sure an exception is not thrown.

Please note that to correctly run pex on the `[PexAssumeUnderTest]` attribute, you need pex to run in instrumentation mode.--------------------